### Compile JavaScript to Hermes Bytecode (`hermesc`)

Source: https://context7.com/discord/hermes/llms.txt

Demonstrates using the standalone Hermes compiler (`hermesc`) to convert JavaScript files into Hermes bytecode (`.hbc`). Supports optimization and embedding debug information. Includes steps for cross-compilation.

```shell
# Compile JS to bytecode with optimizations (default)
./build/bin/hermesc -emit-binary -out output.hbc input.js

# Compile with debug information embedded
./build/bin/hermesc -emit-binary -g -out output.hbc input.js

# Cross-compilation two-stage build: first build the host compiler
cmake -S hermes -B ./build
cmake --build ./build --target hermesc

# Then pass it to the target build via:
# -DIMPORT_HOST_COMPILERS:PATH=$HERMES_WS_DIR/build/ImportHostCompilers.cmake
```

