### SqliteDialectConfig and SqliteDatabase interface

Source: https://github.com/kysely-org/kysely/blob/master/src/dialect/sqlite/sqlite-dialect-config.ts

The SqliteDialectConfig accepts a single `database` option typed as `SqliteDatabase`, an interface modeled after better-sqlite3's API. Any SQLite driver (better-sqlite3, bun:sqlite, node:sqlite) can be used as long as it satisfies this interface (close, prepare returning reader/all/run/iterate). no driver-specific options exist for bun:sqlite or node:sqlite.

```typescript
export interface SqliteDialectConfig {
  database:
    | SqliteDatabase
    | ((options?: AbortableOperationOptions) => Promise<SqliteDatabase>)

  onCreateConnection?: (
    connection: DatabaseConnection,
    options?: AbortableOperationOptions,
  ) => Promise<void>
}

/**
 * This interface is the subset of better-sqlite3 driver's `Database` class that
 * kysely needs.
 *
 * We don't use the type from `better-sqlite3` here to not have a dependency to it.
 */
export interface SqliteDatabase {
  close(): void
  prepare(sql: string): SqliteStatement
}

export interface SqliteStatement {
  readonly reader: boolean
  all(parameters: ReadonlyArray<unknown>): unknown[]
  run(parameters: ReadonlyArray<unknown>): {
    changes: number | bigint
    lastInsertRowid: number | bigint
  }
  iterate(parameters: ReadonlyArray<unknown>): IterableIterator<unknown>
}
```

